# Quality Gates

Before finalizing any change, validate these checks:

## Technical Checks

- New/updated code follows existing route-component-data architecture.
- No unnecessary `"use client"` boundaries were introduced.
- TypeScript remains strict-safe (no new `any` without explicit reason).
- Imports use `@/*` alias where applicable.
- Repeated visual values (especially colors/surfaces) are implemented as shared Tailwind tokens, not duplicated arbitrary color classes.

## UI and Content Checks

- New pages follow section-based composition and spacing rhythm.
- Images use `next/image` correctly with intentional sizing.
- External links opening new tabs include `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
- Navigation labels, breadcrumbs, and page headings are consistent.

## Metadata and SEO Checks

- New significant pages include metadata consideration (title/description).
- Dynamic routes using static data include `generateStaticParams` + `notFound()` handling.

## Final Validation

- Run lint and fix introduced issues before completion.
- Do not bypass lint/type checks unless user explicitly asks.
- Keep diffs focused and minimal; avoid unrelated refactors.
